WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.100
Anime Gintama Big Reflection Meeting

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:12.900
Round 1. Look back enthusiastically on the 4 years of Gintama anime.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.100
Big. Reflection. Meeting.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:20.500
So what are you going to reflect on, Patsuan?

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.700
Oh, me?

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:27.750
If I have to reflect on something, it'll be that I'm worried whether the Santa premise is appropriate.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.750
Probably just that.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.900
Take a look at the calender. It's March now. March.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:36.450
What are you talking about? It's the best last episode.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:41.150
The touching line that the cute female lead delivered at the end was the best!

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:44.800
Uh, the last line was “Happy merry last episode,” wasn't it?

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.400
What kind of touching line is that?

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.600
And you're the kind of people who'd ignore others as long as you're happy, aren't you?

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.000
It can't be helped that the last episode is about Santa.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:57.550
Maybe this is what happens when you use the original work for the finale.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:02.900
Who knew there'd be more material after the Onmyoji Arc?

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:09.000
It might've been too simple-minded to follow the usual pattern of making short arcs after long arcs.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.750
Ah. Time's up.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:15.150
* Kagura is using technical wrestling terms which signifies the start
of the match and the possibility of returning the blow.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:12.650
Show me some spirit!

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:13.620
W-wait. Are we really...

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.150
There's room for comeback!

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:19.700
Yes.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:24.200
Point for Sukonbu. Point for Sukonbu.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:25.700
Thank you for the win.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.100
The hell with the win!

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.650
Will you cut it out?!

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:33.000
We already said this is a reflection meeting. Why the hell are we wrestling?!

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.750
Coz, it's a rare opportunity to come to the Sumo Hall.

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:39.600
Can you stop it!? That's such a poor excuse to blow me off!

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.800
Coz, it's a rare opportunity against Shinpachi.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:44.000
What kind of reason is that?!

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.300
Oi, don't start the reflection meeting with just the three of you.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.450
Although we want to complain more than reflect.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.250
Uh, who're you?

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.450
Huh? What’re you talking about?

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:06.550
Well, I don't really remember the names of minor characters who haven't shown up in the past 2 months.

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:08.200
It's.. Oogushi-kun, right?

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.450
That's it.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:12.400
Vice Commander, I understand your feelings.

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:12.400
I'm gonna kill you!

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.450
Please stop that, boss.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:19.800
All of us, including me, are very bitter about the lack of screen time lately.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:25.450
And here I was thinking, as long as the TV series continued for a bit longer, I'd be promoted from a badminton player to an anpanman.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:25.840
* Gintama ended right before Yamazaki's anpanman arc

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.100
Eh? That's a promotion?

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.450
As for Captain Okita, he is also bothered by the recent lack of screen time...

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.250
See?

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:35.150
Sadist? What sadist?

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:41.050
It's like this anime gives more screen time to masochists than sadists.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:41.900
It seems.

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:44.850
I'll become a masochist as well.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.450
Like that kind of little brother role.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:50.200
Sis, sis, please come back.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:53.250
You see? He's doing his best to give up his character.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:54.750
Please, Okita-kun.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:56.400
It's heartbreaking to watch you. Stop acting like that.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.600
Hm, seems like everyone from Shinsengumi is here...

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.400
Except Kondo-san.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.250
Oh, that.

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:08.400
That gorilla who scored plenty of screen time in the last episode.

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:10.950
Why does the Commander get everything?

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:12.900
Uh-oh. We stepped on a land mine.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.650
We pushed a weird button.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:17.500
Well I guess Kondo-san is also here.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:20.600
But since only he showed up in the last episode,

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.000
We asked him to show some generosity...

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:25.450
By appearing as booger.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.100
That's cruel! And it makes no sense!

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.150
I've given up being a human!

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:31.550
Hey, you guys.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:36.450
You keep saying it's a reflection meeting, but how long are you going to keep bickering about the last episode?

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:37.250
Zura!

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.800
It's not Zura, it's Katsura!

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:43.750
Zura, you weren't in the last episode. Didn't you mind?

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.150
Of course not, Leader.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:49.200
I have plenty of screen time in the movie.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:53.900
A mere last episode isn't gonna...

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.450
You're about to cry! You actually care a hell lot!

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:03.100
Now that everyone's here, let's get back on topic.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.600
Holding a Big Reflection Meeting is fine, but...

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:09.000
Do you have anything from the past 4 years to reflect on?

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:12.100
Nope.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.800
Oi! Where the hell did all your drive go?

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:19.550
No matter what, you all need to reflect on 80% of your lives!

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:20.750
But Shinpachi.

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:23.350
201 episodes aired over 4 years.

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:25.950
We've forgotten the details by now.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:30.150
I guess... But you must remember the important parts.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:34.500
Let's start there and reflect on those.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:38.700
For example, the first episode that aired after we got kicked off Golden Time.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:44.750
* A cour is 13 weeks

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:43.130
We were looking back on the first 2 cours,

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:44.750
while we had hotpot.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:51.050
A shared hotpot is a microcosm of life

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:55.700
Who'll be the one to go on the offensive in this quiet calm and grab the first piece of beef,

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:57.850
Oct 5, 2006
Ep 25: A shared hotpot is a microcosm of life

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.050
that’s the problem.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:02.660
Only those with the resolve to be called greedy and gluttonous,

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:08.270
Take note of the surroundings, and make the first move, will have the right to reign over the hotpot!

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.150
In other words, he’ll be the...

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:12.750
Hotpot Shogun!

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:16.000
In this fight, the first...

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.900
the first one who makes the move, wins!

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:20.400
Got it!

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:25.700
Hey, isn't the heat too low?

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:26.550
Wha-?

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.100
The Hotpot Shogun...

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:29.350
is me!

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:32.900
Chopsticks?

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:36.200
No way! Not in that instant...?!

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:42.950
Go! Chopstick Double Missile!

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:47.850
Don't even think about it!

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:50.350
Meat

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:54.150
Heh, the title of Hotpot Shogun is mine.

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:57.850
She's not innocent at all!

00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:01.100
This brat has shirataki coming out her nose!

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:03.500
Kagura, what a scary child!

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.050
Shiver Shiver

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.900
Did you just realize it, boys?

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:13.500
It all started when I made my stomach growl. All the while, I was concentrating on eating my shirataki. It was all an act.

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:19.100
It was a ruse to put all of you greenhorns off guard and take the seat of the Hotpot Shogun.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:22.440
Just bite your fingers and watch

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:22.160
For... For real?

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:27.400
as of all your beloved beef gets devoured by this little girl!

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:34.250
Utter defeat

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:30.950
W- What?!

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:32.400
She's swallowing it in one gulp!

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:34.400
People of the Yato Clan must have monstrous stomachs!

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:42.200
No way...!

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.200
That's right.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:49.100
The "beef" that you've always been eating was all...

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:51.900
Cheap pork!!

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:57.500
At that moment, I felt an uncertainty, and my legs crumbled under me.

00:06:57.500 --> 00:07:00.150
I won't trust anyone... I can't!

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:04.350
I hope you all break the bone in your little toe!

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:08.950
Come to think of it, there was such a thing.

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:11.050
It started with that episode, didn't it?

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:13.050
Now it's become the signature of Gintama.

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:17.150
Rambling on and on with the background only.

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:18.400
Indeed.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:21.050
It was supposed to be a brand new style of performance,

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:23.100
But people see it as irresponsibility.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.300
What? That's nothing but irresponsibility.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:25.950
That's the definition of irresponsibility!

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:28.200
Well, didn't we reflect on that already?

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:29.950
We even spun the house a few times!

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.250
Shall we do it again?

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:39.100
Excuse me! Me, me , me!!

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:41.350
What is it, Kondo-san?

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:43.600
Shinpachi-kun, it's not just the Yorozuya,

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:45.400
we also want to reflect!

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.150
Please let us look back!

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:50.450
Exactly, there're some things we want to reflect on as well.

00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:52.150
Yeah, there are.

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:55.350
If we want to look back on Shinsengumi,

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:56.700
these are probably the parts.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:08:02.450
There's a thin line between strengths and weaknesses

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:14.500
Apr 24, 2008
Ep 103: A thin line between strengths & weaknesses

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:08.650
I see some faces I know.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:15.050
I hope you're prepared to die for joining that side.

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:20.600
Shinsengumi Regulation Article 21...

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:25.850
Those who have been secretly conspiring with the enemy, shall be punished!

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:37.350
I'll take down all of you.

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:41.750
As the First Unit Captain of the Shinsengumi,

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.650
I shall give you your final lesson.

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:49.200
When faced with an enemy who is considerably more powerful,

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:53.950
it’s best to overcome that power with sheer numbers.

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:57.100
Synchronize your breathing.

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:59.400
Build up spirit in your heart and body.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:01.800
When you are at your peak...

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:05.900
Attack at once!!

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:11.200
And...!!

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:26.890
Die.

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:35.400
Use German Suplex on women who ask which is more important, her or your job

00:09:41.650 --> 00:09:45.640
Dec 27, 2007
Ep 87: Use German Suplex on women who ask which is more important, her or your job

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:44.700
I wouldn't call you evil.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.800
You and I are alike.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:48.850
I've also done countless horrible acts.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:55.750
And to top it off, I'm trying to kill the husband of a woman who's dying.

00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:57.050
It's cruel.

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:01.650
I just...

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:07.200
...want the girl I love to be happy.

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:12.500
A life like that is impossible for a guy like me who lives by the sword.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:15.600
I just wanted her to marry a normal guy somewhere,

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:20.300
have kids like everyone else and live a normal life.

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:25.800
That's... all.

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:32.850
A woman's best make up is her smile

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:38.830
Nov 15, 2007
Ep 81: A woman's best make up is her smile

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:40.080
Eeeeh?!

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:41.310
Just... Wait...

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:42.360
Eeeeeeh?!

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:47.900
Isn't this usually when they cut the cake? With the banana?!

00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:49.050
No, no, no, no.

00:10:49.050 --> 00:10:50.200
Something's wrong here.

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:52.100
It's definitely something that's done together but...

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:54.600
Pops, what's going on?!

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:57.750
What's with that thumbs up?!

00:10:57.750 --> 00:10:58.500
You want me to do it?

00:10:58.500 --> 00:10:59.550
Is that what you want?!

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:01.800
Somebody, break that thumb!

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:03.350
You've got to be kidding!

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:05.700
This isn't some perverted video shoot!

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:06.860
* Note : reference to porn actor Kato Taka. Taka means Hawk.

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:06.860
I'm not Kato Taka!

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:09.200
I'm at most Kato Suzume, someone like me.

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:09.200
Suzume means Sparrow.

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:11.800
Even worse, everyone's watching!

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:13.650
Until a minute ago, they focused on their bananas,

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:15.700
but now they want to watch my banana?!

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.850
Shinpachi-kun, save me!

00:11:17.850 --> 00:11:19.160
I'm taking the rest home with me.

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:20.850
Forget the Tupperware!

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:22.500
You don't have to take bananas home!

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:24.900
How domestic can you get?!

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:31.600
Otae-san.

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:35.150
I wanted to see your smiling face one last time.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:39.350
Hey wait a minute!

00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:41.300
The two of you got the cool scenes,

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.200
why was only mine so different!?

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:47.150
Never mind that. I didn't appear at all! Wasn't that mean?

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:51.250
Eh? Yamazaki, do you have something you want to reflect on?

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:52.900
You're so plain, I don't remember.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:54.550
I can hear you.

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:55.550
I get it, I get it.

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:58.400
Let's try and look back on Zaki.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:00.200
Let's reflect.

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:01.600
Alright, something like this...

00:12:01.810 --> 00:12:07.400
What You Want is Not What You Get

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:10.510
June 28, 2007
Ep 62: What You Want is Not What You Get

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:13.560
Hmph, You still have a long way to go.

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:15.630
Alright, the end.

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:16.550
That was short!

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:19.100
Oi, we were quietly watching, but what’s up with you guys?!

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:21.650
Except for this booger, the rest of you don't plan on reflecting at all!

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:24.500
You just wanted to rewatch the scenes where you were acting cool.

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:26.100
Don't call me booger!

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:28.050
What a useless bunch! Stop being so arrogant!

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:31.800
Really, you guys who didn't even get a proper scene in the last episode,

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:33.900
Don't get ahead of yourselves.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:39.200
Stop talking about the last episode!

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:44.350
Tch. Bring it on.

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:45.650
Kill them!

00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:47.150
Kill the useless bunch!

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:48.600
My thoughts exactly!

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:50.250
Die, Hijikata!

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:51.550
What? That's not right.

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:56.050
Er, what?

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:59.250
They started fighting during an old-styled meeting.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:02.450
Speaking of which, I haven't reflected yet.

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:07.550
Joi is ★ JOY

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:07.550
Lyric.Music: DJ.OZURA

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:07.550
Parody of artist, DJ OZMA

00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:11.370
Jan 10, 2008
Ep 88: The most exciting part of a group date
is before it starts

00:13:10.550 --> 00:13:15.350
If you're gonna do it, do it now. Zura.
If you're gonna do it, do it now. Zura.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:18.250
Joi is Joy! Joi is Joy!

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:20.300
Now the chorus!

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:22.750
No! Sing it! Don't sign it!

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:26.650
I know you talk a lot when I'm not around!

00:13:26.650 --> 00:13:27.850
Okay, one more time.

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:29.100
Joy!

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:33.500
Yup, that was some good rap.

00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:37.150
If I have to reflect on it, I'd say I'll spice it up a little,

00:13:37.150 --> 00:13:39.000
and then perform in the Sumo Hall.

00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:40.750
Joy!

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:45.300
There will be no performance! Whatever you're reflecting on is too bizarre!

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:46.250
Don't be jealous, Gintoki.

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:47.600
I'm not jealous!

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:51.200
How am I supposed to clean up this mess?

00:13:52.550 --> 00:13:56.350
And how is this a reflection meeting?

00:13:56.350 --> 00:14:00.150
Is it really appropriate to show this at the event?

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:02.950
Huh? Am I the one reflecting right now?

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:05.400
Eh? That's why it's the reflection meeting?

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:06.150
N-no way.

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:07.970
They can't pull this kind of half-assed ending.

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:14.950
Anime Gintama Big Reflection Meeting END

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:15.650
They really did it!!
